  "description": "Installation of roof mounted solar panels and condenser units and associated works.",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "<p>The development hereby permitted must be begun not later than the expiration of three years beginning with the date of this permission.</p><p><br></p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\nREASON: In order to comply with the provisions of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990 (as amended).</p><p>\r\n</p>",
    "&lt;p&gt;Unless otherwise hereby approved, all new works in respect of all the works hereby approved (and any other incidental works to be carried out in this connection) shall match the existing building in respect of materials used, detailed execution and finished appearance.\r\n\r\n&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;REASON: To ensure a satisfactory external appearance.&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;Prior to the commencement of the relevant part of the development hereby approved, precise details of the acoustic enclosures of the condenser units (to include materials and finishes) shall be submitted to and agreed in writing by the Local Planning Authority. The development shall thereafter be carried out in strict accordance with the details hereby approved.&lt;/p&gt;",
    "<p>The Development hereby permitted shall only be carried out and completed strictly in accordance with the submitted plans hereby approved and any subsequent approval of details.\r\n</p><p><br></p><p>\r\nREASON: To ensure that the development hereby permitted is carried out in full accordance with the plans hereby approved.\r\n</p>",
    "&lt;p&gt;Within 3 months of the operation of any building services plant hereby approved a post-installation noise assessment shall be carried out to confirm compliance with the noise criteria. The scheme shall be implemented in accordance with the approved details and attenuation measures, and they shall be permanently retained and maintained in working order for the duration of the use and their operation.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Reason: To protect the amenities of adjoining occupiers and the surrounding area&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
